    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d1bf5624-bf81-4d21-9190-6ecfd114fedb-a7eb5601-62c0-4b97-b2d2-7b026607e965-9895383.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 204px;\" /></p><p>Point D and G are at same potential. Same is the case with point E and F.</p><p>Now, resistance between DC and GC are in parallel combination. Similarly, resistance between CE and CF are in parallel combination. The modified circuit will be as shown below considering&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for parallel combination.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cdc02fbc-5891-4e5c-8043-eaee2132947e-9895383_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 190px;\" /></p><p>Therefore, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>&#937;</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
